WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.100
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.105 --> 00:01.105
MkvDrama.net

3
00:26.225 --> 00:28.195
It's already past noon.

4
00:29.325 --> 00:31.485
Who cares? It's summer vacation anyway.

5
00:32.895 --> 00:36.895
But we have to pack for band camp.

6
00:41.505 --> 00:44.345
I really don't feel like going.

7
00:44.705 --> 00:45.575
Huh?

8
00:45.645 --> 00:47.775
Weren't you looking forward to it?

9
00:48.255 --> 00:50.064
Well, it's a group trip, right?

10
00:50.065 --> 00:52.715
If I can't be alone with you, Miwa, what's the point?

11
00:53.345 --> 00:57.785
I wanted to cuddle and make out and do naughty things out in nature.

12
00:59.855 --> 01:03.055
Your mind is in the gutter again.

13
01:07.065 --> 01:10.135
Come on, Miwa, you like that stuff too, don't you?

14
01:13.735 --> 01:15.605
Wait, hold on...

15
01:18.345 --> 01:19.575
Just for a second.

16
01:20.075 --> 01:21.075
Please?

17
01:30.825 --> 01:32.055
Saeko, really...

18
01:35.025 --> 01:36.455
I'll pass.

19
02:30.805 --> 02:38.305
"How Do We Relationship?"

20
02:42.855 --> 02:43.655
We're here.

21
02:43.656 --> 02:45.576
[Episode 3: I Don't Get Jealous] Finally made it!

22
02:46.125 --> 02:47.125
Man, this is so heavy!

23
02:47.245 --> 02:48.504
I'll go get the keys.

24
02:48.505 --> 02:49.735
Here, let me take that.

25
02:49.765 --> 02:51.135
- Oh, thanks. - Sure.

26
02:54.775 --> 02:56.244
My sunglasses are missing, too.

27
02:56.245 --> 02:58.224
Did you leave them in the car?

28
02:58.225 --> 02:59.884
- Did you see them? - Nope.

29
02:59.885 --> 03:03.215
Look, we're not here on vacation.

30
03:03.485 --> 03:06.024
Even if you're the lead singer, at least help carry some gear.

31
03:06.025 --> 03:07.224
But they're my sunglasses!

32
03:07.225 --> 03:08.225
How should I know?

33
03:08.305 --> 03:09.305
Right, Saeko?

34
03:17.095 --> 03:20.025
Saeko, don't you ever get jealous?

35
03:20.685 --> 03:21.695
Huh?

36
03:21.985 --> 03:23.964
Why would Miwa suddenly fall for a guy now?

37
03:23.965 --> 03:27.335
No, but even if you know she'd never cheat...

38
03:27.365 --> 03:30.334
Wouldn't you still get mad seeing her get so cozy with someone else?

39
03:30.335 --> 03:31.335
Whoa, that's heavy.

40
03:33.005 --> 03:34.075
What's wrong with heavy?

41
03:34.105 --> 03:36.325
Hi there, I'm the suffocating control freak.

42
03:36.405 --> 03:38.065
A clingy monster.

43
03:38.485 --> 03:40.315
No thanks, count me out.

44
03:40.365 --> 03:43.221
That stuff is exhausting, whether you're controlling someone or being controlled.

45
03:43.245 --> 03:45.704
I've gotten into fights over jealousy before, too.

46
03:45.705 --> 03:50.255
See? Your girlfriend might dump you one day, too.

47
03:50.855 --> 03:52.794
We're madly in love, thank you very much.

48
03:52.795 --> 03:54.025
Really?

49
03:54.365 --> 03:56.645
With a face like that, you're definitely too suffocating.

50
03:57.865 --> 03:59.404
Hey, now I'm pissed!

51
03:59.405 --> 04:00.844
Oh? You wanna go?

52
04:00.845 --> 04:02.174
- Here they go. - Wait!

53
04:02.175 --> 04:03.574
Possessive chokehold!

54
04:03.575 --> 04:04.365
Nice one!

55
04:04.366 --> 04:05.644
Count it for me, Mikkun!

56
04:05.645 --> 04:07.945
Three! Two! One!

57
04:07.975 --> 04:11.085
- You're making Miwa uncomfortable. - Yeah, she looks troubled. Knock it off.

58
04:22.385 --> 04:23.984
Alright, let's wrap it up for today.

59
04:23.985 --> 04:25.134
Thanks, good job everyone.

60
04:25.135 --> 04:26.844
Miwa, right after the pre-chorus...

61
04:26.845 --> 04:27.855
Miwa.

62
04:28.665 --> 04:29.665
Hmm?

63
04:30.225 --> 04:31.745
Let's head back to the room for a sec.

64
04:35.605 --> 04:36.935
What's up?

65
04:37.175 --> 04:38.885
Huh? I forgot something.

66
04:48.315 --> 04:49.455
Miwa.

67
04:49.615 --> 04:50.615
Yeah?

68
05:02.035 --> 05:03.325
Miwa, do you...

69
05:04.505 --> 05:06.165
Do you ever get jealous or anything?

70
05:07.305 --> 05:08.305
Huh?

71
05:09.105 --> 05:10.304
Where is this coming from?

72
05:10.305 --> 05:11.305
Nothing, just...

73
05:11.985 --> 05:16.045
You saw me messing around with Lucha and the guys earlier, right?

74
05:17.415 --> 05:18.815
I was wondering if it bothered you.

75
05:22.915 --> 05:27.795
I don't think I'd be like that.

76
05:30.195 --> 05:32.365
I trust you, Saeko.

77
05:32.465 --> 05:34.495
I don't think I'd get jealous.

78
05:39.735 --> 05:41.005
Same here.

79
05:41.635 --> 05:43.184
Then we're on the same page.

80
05:43.185 --> 05:44.675
Saeko, wait, hold on...

81
06:00.325 --> 06:06.565
And besides... I want you to feel free, Saeko.

82
06:08.135 --> 06:10.095
So I don't want to tie you down.

83
06:26.485 --> 06:27.645
Is something wrong?

84
06:31.125 --> 06:32.125
It's nothing.

85
06:32.785 --> 06:35.795
Just surprised at how compatible we are.

86
06:40.295 --> 06:41.365
Let's head back.

87
06:44.135 --> 06:45.465
Saeko?

88
06:50.535 --> 06:52.151
This still looks a bit rare. Sorry about that.

89
06:52.175 --> 06:54.445
I'll go grab some more.

90
06:56.715 --> 06:59.085
Shouldn't you go hang out with Miwa?

91
06:59.845 --> 07:00.845
It's fine.

92
07:01.055 --> 07:03.855
I feel bad monopolizing her time.

93
07:04.655 --> 07:06.025
Oh?

94
07:06.325 --> 07:08.555
What are you pouting about?

95
07:09.575 --> 07:11.195
I'm not pouting!

96
07:11.935 --> 07:14.935
Besides, Miwa told me she doesn't get jealous over me.

97
07:15.195 --> 07:16.865
We both give each other plenty of space.

98
07:18.595 --> 07:21.415
Saeko, you're so annoying today.

99
07:21.975 --> 07:24.035
What? What did you say?

100
07:24.875 --> 07:26.245
Ah, wait!

101
07:27.235 --> 07:29.875
Saeko, if you have a minute, could you run an errand for us?

102
07:30.745 --> 07:32.685
- She's definitely not free! - Ah, wait a second.

103
07:33.075 --> 07:35.055
Hey, wait up! Rika! Seriously!

104
07:35.885 --> 07:37.925
Saeko, please? I can't step away right now.

105
07:38.833 --> 07:40.260
- Fine, if you insist. - Sorry about that.

106
07:40.285 --> 07:41.625
Thanks, I really appreciate it!

107
07:48.415 --> 07:50.865
Saeko, I'll come with you.

108
07:51.335 --> 07:53.175
You don't have to. Go hang out with everyone.

109
07:53.565 --> 07:54.565
No.

110
07:54.705 --> 07:56.635
I want to go with you.

111
08:01.245 --> 08:02.245
Alright then.

112
08:02.715 --> 08:03.875
Guess I'll let you tag along.

113
08:05.085 --> 08:09.615
This is ridiculously heavy! Did they seriously expect me to carry all this alone?

114
08:09.855 --> 08:11.954
Aren't you glad the two of us came together?

115
08:11.955 --> 08:13.575
Well, yeah, I guess.

116
08:14.455 --> 08:15.795
But it's so hot!

117
08:16.815 --> 08:18.224
- Sorry, sorry. Here. - Want me to carry that for you?

118
08:18.225 --> 08:19.625
What are you two up to?

119
08:20.355 --> 08:21.394
Need a hand?

120
08:21.395 --> 08:22.451
Want us to carry that for you?

121
08:22.475 --> 08:24.194
- Let us take it! - Wanna eat some corn with us?

122
08:24.195 --> 08:25.594
- You okay? - We're in a hurry.

123
08:25.595 --> 08:27.491
At least give us your Insta, then! Just your Insta!

124
08:27.515 --> 08:29.075
Come on, hook us up!

125
08:29.115 --> 08:30.115
Please, pretty please?

126
08:30.615 --> 08:32.345
What's the harm? Come on!

127
08:32.555 --> 08:33.831
Please, just your handle! What's the big deal? What's the big deal?

128
08:33.855 --> 08:34.955
Come on, please?

129
08:34.975 --> 08:36.015
- Pretty please? - Wait up!

130
08:36.935 --> 08:40.045
- Let's go. - It's just Insta! What's the problem?

131
08:51.595 --> 08:53.865
What was their problem?

132
08:53.995 --> 08:55.135
That really ticked me off.

133
08:58.915 --> 08:59.915
I'm sorry.

134
09:00.975 --> 09:03.605
Saeko, you ended up carrying my stuff too.

135
09:03.775 --> 09:06.295
That's what you get for being too cute.

136
09:06.315 --> 09:10.345
You total knockout, femme fatale, heartbreaker.

137
09:11.195 --> 09:12.715
Are those supposed to be insults?

138
09:15.355 --> 09:17.385
All that running wiped me out.

139
09:17.815 --> 09:21.395
Whatever, I'm cracking one of these open.

140
09:27.055 --> 09:28.055
I'm really sorry.

141
09:29.775 --> 09:34.815
I wish I could handle guys like that as well as you do.

142
09:36.275 --> 09:37.535
No kidding.

143
09:37.575 --> 09:39.305
Why were you being so polite to them?

144
09:39.715 --> 09:41.645
You've gotta protect yourself.

145
09:45.835 --> 09:48.055
I'm just kidding.

146
09:48.215 --> 09:51.155
That helpless side of you is pretty cute, too.

147
09:53.235 --> 09:55.935
Anyway, you're carrying the bags on the way back.

148
09:55.975 --> 09:57.765
I'm completely exhausted.

149
09:58.825 --> 10:00.625
Um, Saeko...

150
10:00.655 --> 10:03.465
We're sprinting all the way back!

151
10:09.755 --> 10:10.835
Saeko!

152
10:20.015 --> 10:22.794
What's going on so early in the morning?

153
10:22.795 --> 10:27.025
- Apparently, his girlfriend just dumped him. - What?!

154
10:27.575 --> 10:29.695
Didn't he just say yesterday they were crazy in love?

155
10:29.825 --> 10:32.165
She dumped him over the phone out of nowhere.

156
10:33.555 --> 10:35.795
He can't perform like this!

157
10:35.955 --> 10:37.035
What do we do?

158
10:37.265 --> 10:38.365
Lucha.

159
10:38.965 --> 10:42.535
Keep your head up! Today's our debut gig as freshmen!

160
10:45.755 --> 10:47.005
Sorry, Saeko.

161
10:47.375 --> 10:49.445
- Can you cover lead vocals too? - Huh?

162
10:50.145 --> 10:51.515
I told you, there's no way!

163
10:51.875 --> 10:53.515
Hey, Lucha...

164
10:56.475 --> 10:57.475
Kaori...

165
10:58.795 --> 11:03.155
I was jealous and controlling...

166
11:05.495 --> 11:09.995
I just wanted your eyes on me and no one else!

167
11:12.665 --> 11:13.665
Um...

168
11:15.135 --> 11:18.775
Can't we just tell them we can't play this time?

169
11:18.975 --> 11:20.575
I mean, under the circumstances...

170
11:23.545 --> 11:25.315
It's all my fault...

171
11:28.315 --> 11:29.315
Forget it...

172
11:30.635 --> 11:32.155
Forget it, I'll do it.

173
11:32.985 --> 11:34.895
I'll handle both vocals and guitar.

174
11:35.495 --> 11:36.495
What?

175
11:36.855 --> 11:37.865
Saeko...

176
11:39.655 --> 11:40.825
Are you sure you can do this?

177
11:41.475 --> 11:42.475
I've got this.

178
11:42.865 --> 11:44.035
I'll make it work.

179
11:47.455 --> 11:48.455
Um...

180
11:49.075 --> 11:52.245
If there's anything I can do to help...

181
11:54.245 --> 11:56.115
Then why don't you sing in my place, Miwa?

182
12:00.755 --> 12:02.785
Just kidding. I'm joking.

183
12:03.935 --> 12:05.625
I need to focus on my own.

184
12:06.715 --> 12:07.855
Sorry.

185
12:39.505 --> 12:40.505
Are you okay?

186
12:58.245 --> 12:59.905
Are you worried about Saeko?

187
13:03.415 --> 13:05.715
It's not just worry.

188
13:07.125 --> 13:08.125
I just feel like...

189
13:08.745 --> 13:12.285
Like there's nothing I can do for her.

190
13:13.745 --> 13:17.025
She's always the one helping me.

191
13:20.625 --> 13:24.465
True. Saeko's the type who handles everything on her own.

192
13:26.305 --> 13:28.635
She's not the kind of person who leans on others.

193
13:29.605 --> 13:31.205
That might be true, but...

194
13:33.605 --> 13:34.605
I...

195
13:35.145 --> 13:39.685
I feel like if things stay this way, I'll let Saeko down sooner or later.

196
13:41.025 --> 13:42.855
Or maybe I already have.

197
13:42.885 --> 13:44.825
No way. You're overthinking it.

198
13:45.355 --> 13:47.485
I want to change.

199
13:48.125 --> 13:49.805
I want to become strong, just like Saeko.

200
13:50.855 --> 13:53.925
Maybe she's just putting on a brave face, you know?

201
13:54.165 --> 13:55.165
Oh.

202
13:55.295 --> 13:56.235
Rika.

203
13:56.295 --> 14:00.305
Tsuruta, the sound guy wants to talk about the live set.

204
14:00.905 --> 14:02.605
Oh, I'll be right there.

205
14:06.245 --> 14:07.245
Miwa.

206
14:07.825 --> 14:09.615
Don't beat yourself up.

207
14:22.025 --> 14:24.825
Sorry, Saeko. We always dump everything on you.

208
14:25.365 --> 14:26.725
It's fine, don't sweat it.

209
14:26.845 --> 14:29.735
Just don't get mad at me if I mess up out there.

210
14:33.865 --> 14:39.245
The next band originally had Lucha on lead vocals...

211
14:39.325 --> 14:45.185
but he got dumped and can't sing, so Saeko's filling in today!

212
14:51.885 --> 14:53.825
Alright, let's do this!

213
14:56.145 --> 14:58.525
- Yeah! - I'm so nervous!

214
15:11.105 --> 15:12.105
Okay.

215
15:57.925 --> 16:01.355
♪ The sky dyed in vermilion ♪

216
16:01.395 --> 16:04.765
♪ Whispers of the night ♪

217
16:04.825 --> 16:08.435
♪ Driving us forward today ♪

218
16:08.535 --> 16:12.664
♪ Ever onward ♪

219
16:12.665 --> 16:19.775
♪ Our song, blurred by dazzling lights ♪

220
16:20.005 --> 16:24.645
♪ As we hum it softly ♪

221
16:25.345 --> 16:29.005
♪ Blending together, easing the weight ♪

222
16:29.045 --> 16:32.545
♪ Once discovered, we fled into this place ♪

223
16:32.945 --> 16:36.095
♪ Remembering the times we laughed ♪

224
16:36.155 --> 16:39.664
♪ We're missing ♪

225
16:39.665 --> 16:43.334
♪ Jewels inside the soda ♪

226
16:43.335 --> 16:46.795
♪ Gold coins left unspent ♪

227
16:46.835 --> 16:50.635
♪ A blade so easily snapped ♪

228
16:50.705 --> 16:53.845
♪ A feather hairpin ♪

229
16:54.205 --> 16:57.845
♪ A lone droplet drifting ♪

230
16:57.885 --> 17:01.585
♪ Like our slim odds of winning ♪

231
17:01.685 --> 17:05.154
♪ And a warm blanket ♪

232
17:05.155 --> 17:08.004
♪ These are all precious, too ♪

233
17:08.005 --> 17:11.465
♪ Blending together, easing the weight ♪

234
17:11.585 --> 17:15.475
♪ Once discovered, we fled into this place ♪

235
17:15.525 --> 17:18.805
♪ Remembering the times we laughed ♪

236
17:18.835 --> 17:22.575
♪ We're missing ♪

237
17:22.725 --> 17:26.345
♪ Made mistakes and lost a few things ♪

238
17:26.375 --> 17:29.945
♪ Wandering lost, I found you again ♪

239
17:29.975 --> 17:33.485
♪ Remembering the times we laughed ♪

240
17:33.515 --> 17:36.255
♪ We're missing ♪

241
17:36.305 --> 17:42.255
♪ We're missing ♪

242
17:44.825 --> 17:48.495
♪ Ever since you've been gone... ♪

243
17:49.295 --> 17:54.504
Isn't that a bit harsh? Come on, next up! Let's go!

244
17:54.505 --> 17:56.034
The upperclassmen were totally amazing earlier!

245
17:56.035 --> 17:58.605
Cheers!

246
17:59.705 --> 18:02.304
Hey, where did Saeko and Miwa go?

247
18:02.305 --> 18:03.515
Huh?

248
18:05.405 --> 18:06.405
Hey, Saeko.

249
18:07.105 --> 18:08.315
What is going on with you?

250
18:08.845 --> 18:10.485
You've been acting weird this whole time.

251
18:15.785 --> 18:17.765
Why do you keep pushing me away?

252
18:19.175 --> 18:20.275
I don't know.

253
18:21.945 --> 18:23.665
What do you mean, you don't know?

254
18:26.045 --> 18:29.075
Do you hate me now?

255
18:29.605 --> 18:30.635
What?

256
18:31.605 --> 18:32.965
Why on earth would you think that?

257
18:34.955 --> 18:35.995
I can't take this anymore.

258
18:36.335 --> 18:37.715
I can't think straight.

259
18:38.955 --> 18:40.115
Let's do it, Miwa.

260
18:40.395 --> 18:41.395
Wait, Saeko...

261
18:55.995 --> 18:59.065
Saeko, what's gotten into you?

262
19:05.495 --> 19:07.545
It's okay. You can leave a mark.

263
19:09.135 --> 19:10.775
As long as it's somewhere nobody can see.

264
19:12.085 --> 19:13.145
You knew?

265
19:15.755 --> 19:16.755
Yeah.

266
19:22.875 --> 19:23.875
I'm sorry.

267
19:27.425 --> 19:28.495
Saeko.

268
19:34.435 --> 19:35.475
I'm sorry.

269
19:43.415 --> 19:45.495
It's my fault, isn't it?

270
19:48.835 --> 19:51.825
Because I'm so unreliable, it made you insecure, didn't it?

271
19:51.955 --> 19:53.385
You didn't do anything wrong.

272
19:55.625 --> 19:57.395
I'm just being childish.

273
19:59.025 --> 20:03.595
I was feeling frustrated and ended up taking it out on you.

274
20:07.075 --> 20:08.805
Is that really all it was?

275
20:15.115 --> 20:18.515
Maybe because we kept getting interrupted ever since we got here.

276
20:19.745 --> 20:21.855
So I got sexually frustrated, probably.

277
20:27.015 --> 20:30.195
Then... do you want to...?

278
20:34.115 --> 20:36.365
Wait, no! That's definitely not why.

279
20:36.715 --> 20:39.964
I was treating you so horribly just now.

280
20:39.965 --> 20:41.335
And I hurt you.

281
20:42.805 --> 20:43.805
Honestly...

282
20:44.405 --> 20:47.005
I'm not nearly as hurt as you think, Saeko.

283
20:48.975 --> 20:56.185
And if you want to do it too, Saeko, then I...

284
20:58.655 --> 21:00.685
What do you mean, "if you want to too"?

285
21:13.235 --> 21:17.305
Don't you think that makes me awful?

286
21:19.155 --> 21:20.375
Does it?

287
21:20.445 --> 21:21.715
Yes, it does.

288
21:23.695 --> 21:26.645
But it's also wonderfully sweet.

289
21:31.225 --> 21:32.455
So pretty.

290
21:32.825 --> 21:35.155
Please turn into Kaori!

291
21:36.155 --> 21:38.665
What took you guys so long? What were you doing?

292
21:38.825 --> 21:41.465
Can't you just become Kaori?

293
21:42.565 --> 21:43.965
Let's join in too!

294
21:46.475 --> 21:48.635
Oh, let's light sparklers!

295
21:49.175 --> 21:51.544
First one whose spark drops loses, okay?

296
21:51.545 --> 21:52.545
Okay.

297
22:17.705 --> 22:21.775
Remember when I said I wasn't hurt?

298
22:23.005 --> 22:24.005
Yeah.

299
22:25.115 --> 22:29.045
That was half a lie.

300
22:29.645 --> 22:30.645
Huh?

301
22:34.385 --> 22:35.715
I actually felt really lonely.

302
22:38.295 --> 22:41.055
Wondering if you hated me...

303
22:42.255 --> 22:44.055
I was really insecure.

304
22:48.735 --> 22:51.405
Ah, Saeko lost!

305
22:53.335 --> 22:55.335
I'm always insecure, too.

306
22:56.055 --> 22:59.975
I worry that you'll hate me, too, so scared I can't even fall asleep at night.

307
23:01.115 --> 23:04.375
Come on, now you're bluffing again.

308
23:07.755 --> 23:08.785
Must be nice.

309
23:09.385 --> 23:11.325
You can be so honest about your feelings, Miwa.

310
23:13.395 --> 23:14.395
What?

311
23:19.495 --> 23:21.995
Miwa, look! Dual wielding!

312
